cff-version: 1.2.0
title: A systematics audit of the magnetic limb-darkening result
message: If you use this audit or its numbers, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Pragyaan
    family-names: Gaur
    email: pragyaangaur12@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/pragyaangaur/Magnetic-Limb-Darkening-Audit
abstract: An independent systematics audit of Kostogryz et al. (2024), who attribute the offset between observed and modelled stellar limb darkening to small-scale surface magnetic fields. The audit finds that the h1 half of the result is stable under reanalysis, and that the h2 half is the size of an analysis systematic measured and flagged by Maxted (2023), the paper the observed values come from. A metallicity scale error is excluded as a non-magnetic explanation and facular coverage of the transit chord is unlikely, while a temperature scale error of about 200 K cannot yet be excluded. Every number is regenerated from published data by the scripts in this repository.
keywords:
  - limb darkening
  - stellar atmospheres
  - transiting exoplanets
  - solar magnetic fields
  - systematics
license: BSD-3-Clause
date-released: "2026-09-05"
